EXTRA QUESTIONS
Q: Supervised vs unsupervised learning?
A: Supervised learning uses labelled examples; unsupervised learning finds patterns without labels.

Q: Why can K-Means give different results?
A: Results can depend on initial centroid positions. Multiple initializations and a fixed random_state improve consistency.

Q: What is one limitation of K-Means?
A: It requires the number of clusters in advance and can be affected by outliers and feature scales.

Q: Why is feature scaling often used with K-Means?
A: K-Means uses distances, so features with larger ranges can dominate. This code does not scale the Iris features.
